# ----------------------------------------------------------
# ::: [ LISKA PACKAGE MANAGER MIRRORLIST CONFIGURATION ] :::
# ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# This file configures repository URLs rules for lkpm.
#
# > Sections: [core] | [extra]
#
# > [core] section are the most prioritized repo for lkpm running
#   smoothly. The [core] packages cant get overwrited by [extra] 
#   section to ensure system stability. If you change the [core] 
#   URLs, made sure you know what you are doing.
#
# > [extra] section are used for custom repository a.k.a Liska User
#   Repository and will get called by lkpm if the packages not
#   exits on the [core] section. Made sure the custom repository 
#   host tar files (.tar, .tar.zst, .tar.gz, or .tar.xz) and have 
#   package metadata like .PKGINFO or .BUILDINFO.
#
# > NOTE: Changes take effect the next time "lkpm" is called 
#         (no daemon restart) using "lkpm -r".
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------


